## Summary

Shipped the **`BatteryComparison`** Apple feature view (P4 · 0275) — a production-polished SwiftUI parity of `web/src/features/vehicles/components/BatteryComparison.tsx` (the "Fleet Battery Status" panel: per-vehicle battery bars with name, level %, and rated range).

**7 files** committed to `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/` (`97ff3efae`):
- `.Adapter.swift` — pure Foundation core: `batteryColor` tint thresholds, SI `formatDistance` port (1000/1609.344 factors, precision 1, em-dash), clamped fill fraction, null-state-filtering projection, phase/status/connection, a11y.
- `.Model.swift` — P1/S8 source seam + `@Observable` model, P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry, P1/S10 strings facade, stale auto-refresh, in-memory source.
- `.Views.swift` — Activity-glyph header, freshness chip, connectivity banner, gradient+glow fill track, bar rows, and loading/empty/error states.
- `.swift` — `TSGlassPanel` shell + phase switch + lifecycle + a11y.
- `.Previews.swift` (6 states), `.Tests.swift` (30 tests), `.strings` (i18n table).

